  "function": "plan_tracking",
  "note": "Plan tracking, by hand (docs/08 section 11, rules 1 to 3), with an on-plan tolerance of 5%. Plan 'worked' is worked example 1 with two more years: 2025-12-31 has no net debt and 2026-12-31 no EBITDA. Case 1, the worked example: 2024-06-30 is day 182 of 366, so revenue 200,000,000 + 36,600,000 x 182 / 366 = 218,200,000, EBITDA 43,640,000 and net debt 146,360,000, each interpolated; revenue 220,000,000 is +1,800,000, +0.0082493126, on plan; EBITDA 40,500,000 is -3,140,000, -0.0719523373, behind; net debt 150,000,000 is +3,640,000, 0.0248701831 over, so -2.49% favourable, on plan. Case 2, on a plan date (not interpolated): revenue 248,430,000 is 236,600,000 x 1.05, exactly on the edge, on plan; EBITDA 49,686,000.01 is a cent over 47,320,000 x 1.05, 0.0500000002, ahead; net debt 135,546,000 is 142,680,000 x 0.95, 5% under plan and exactly on the favourable edge, on plan. Case 3, a line that does not terminate: 2025-03-31 is day 90 of 365, revenue 236,600,000 + 33,400,000 x 90 / 365 = 244,835,616.4383561644 at ten places and EBITDA 47,320,000 + 7,680,000 x 90 / 365 = 49,213,698.6301369863; the variance is the actual less the plan as held, to the last place; net debt has no figure at 2025-12-31, so none here, and the 2026 point is not used in its place. Case 4: on 2025-12-31 itself the point has no net debt; EBITDA 60,500,000 is 10% over 55,000,000, ahead. Case 5: 2026-06-30 is day 181 of 365; revenue 270,000,000 + 30,000,000 x 181 / 365 = 284,876,712.3287671233; EBITDA has no figure at 2026-12-31 and net debt none at 2025-12-31. Case 6 is before the plan starts and case 7 after it ends: the actuals stand, the plan does not. Case 8: no revenue in the quarter (the plan figure still stands); an EBITDA of -2,000,000 is -45,640,000 against 43,640,000, behind; net debt 131,724,000 is 10% under plan, ahead. Case 9: no current quarter. Case 10, the low edges: EBITDA 41,458,000 is 43,640,000 x 0.95, on plan; revenue 207,289,999.99 is a cent under 218,200,000 x 0.95, -0.0500000000458 before it is held and -0.05 at ten places, so on plan (the status is judged on the percent as it travels); net debt 160,996,000 is 10% over plan, behind. Case 11: revenue 207,289,999.00 is a dollar under the edge, -0.0500000046, behind; EBITDA 41,457,999.99 is a cent under it, -0.0500000002, behind; net debt 153,678,000 is 5% over plan, on the unfavourable edge, on plan. Plan 'netCash' runs from net debt of 5,000,000 on 2023-12-31 to net cash of 5,000,000 on 2024-06-30. Case 12: 2024-03-31 is day 91 of 182, so the planned net debt is exactly 0: the variance of +1,000,000 stands and there is no percent; revenue 55,000,000 is the plan, 0, on plan; EBITDA 12,100,000 against 11,000,000 is +10%, ahead. Case 13: on 2024-06-30 the plan is net cash of 5,000,000 and the actual net cash of 8,000,000, a variance of -3,000,000 and no percent. Case 14: a plan with no points has no figure.",
